      "subject": "fix(tests): every governed store is isolated per test process (F-25)",
      "body": "Without KORELUMINA_CANONICAL_ROOT and KORELUMINA_ACTIVATION_ROOT, tests wrote into the repository's real canonical items and Chief Agent activation records, so running the suite could add test items to the Chief Agent's governed knowledge. Executive and learning stores used the working directory and knowledge storage a per-pid folder inside the repository, so tests read each other's leftovers and failed depending on order. In test processes every governed store (knowledge, canonical items, activation, executive, continuous learning) now uses a fresh temporary directory, removed on exit; Runtime itself is unaffected. Four tests that assumed the old locations or an empty shared store now check their own records. Result without any environment variables: executive, routes, learning, knowledge platform, canonical knowledge and runtime suites 409/409, the repository's runtime stores byte-for-byte unchanged; the 10 remaining knowledge-preservation failures were already failing (F-30).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AHtXdN7VRusNxTFHzk5uFe",
